	"_comment": "UNDERROOT - the caves beneath the great tree. A walk-and-wonder cave (no goal, no enemies, no fail states): twisting root tunnels and nine chambers in the dark, where you see only a small soft circle round yourself (atmosphere.fog, MistVeil as a darkness) and glow-moss, glowcaps and your companion's own light thin it into pockets. Nine regions: the Rootfall (where you arrive), the Tangle, the Drip Hall, the Hush Pools, the Glowcap Garden, the Lantern Room, the Old Stair, Cairn Row and the Heartwood. The tunnel walls are 'hedges' (axis-aligned segments the nav grid already understands) drawn as roots through the art block's hedge tile. It RE-SKINS ITSELF through its 'art' block (deep-merged over data/art.json). Its secret is the root-heart: see the 'secret' block (reveal type 'follow': ask your companion to Go look and follow its light). Generated by tools/gen_underroot_world.py (art: pokepals/tools/gen_underroot.py) - edit that and re-run, don't hand-tune positions. Maze seed 1728, 57 cells from the arrival to the heart.",
